---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Sayumarketing"
  description="From an agency with no consistent sales to its first two clients within the first month of work, by revisiting positioning, offer, pricing and commercial communication."
>
  <article class="section" style="padding-top: 100px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label" style="color: var(--gold)">Strategic Collaboration · Marketing agency</p>
      <h1 class="display" style="font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 64px); margin: 16px 0 40px">Sayumarketing</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The context</h2>
        <p>Sayumarketing had been operating as an agency for about a year, but hadn't yet turned its activity into consistent client acquisition.</p>
        <h2>The diagnosis</h2>
        <p>The problem wasn't simply doing more marketing. The agency's commercial foundations needed a review: positioning, value proposition, offer, pricing and communication.</p>
        <h2>The intervention</h2>
        <p>I worked with the team to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Redefine positioning</li>
          <li>Structure the value proposition</li>
          <li>Review pricing</li>
          <li>Organize the offer</li>
          <li>Improve commercial communication</li>
          <li>Point the strategy toward clearer client acquisition</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>The result</h2>
        <p>During the first month of work, Sayumarketing landed its first two clients.</p>
        <p>The change didn't start by doing more marketing. It started by better understanding what was being sold, to whom, and why it should be chosen over any other option.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/en/contacto" class="btn" style="margin-top: 40px; display: inline-block">Let's talk about your project →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose :global(h2) { font-size: 26px; margin: 40px 0 12px; }
  .prose :global(p) { margin: 0 0 16px; }
</style>
